WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.080
Audiences will be cast back into the&nbsp;
fires of Panem with "The Hunger Games:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:08.560
The Ballad of Songbirds &amp; Snakes." Here's&nbsp;
everything you can expect from the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.080
from who's starring to where&nbsp;
it fits into the story.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.080
Fans haven't enjoyed a new "Hunger&nbsp;
Games" movie since "The Hunger Games:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:21.240
Mockingjay — Part 2" hit theaters in 2015.&nbsp;
Thankfully, they don't have much longer to wait:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:27.360
"The Hunger Games: The Ballad of Songbirds &amp;&nbsp;
Snakes" is set to debut on November 17, 2023.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.000
It seems like a long wait for fans&nbsp;
of the franchise, but this movie has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.920
actually made a relatively speedy journey&nbsp;
to the big screen. The book it's based on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:40.040
Suzanne Collins' "The Ballad of Songbirds and&nbsp;
Snakes," was released in 2020. That's a pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:46.040
swift turnaround between publication and cinematic&nbsp;
adaptation, even for a blockbuster franchise. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:51.040
timeline is even more impressive when you take&nbsp;
the COVID-19 pandemic into account: The crisis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:56.280
hit mere months before the book was launched,&nbsp;
spoiling all hopes of real-world tours and events.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:01.320
As the pandemic ground on, the movie's production&nbsp;
schedule was doubtlessly impacted — yet the powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:07.120
that be still managed to get it cast, planned,&nbsp;
filmed, edited, and ready to go in just a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.560
years. Even the most eager fans can appreciate&nbsp;
that sort of flexibility and determination.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.480
In "The Ballad of Songbirds&nbsp;
&amp; Snakes," Coriolanus Snow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.720
the fiendish despot who menaces Katniss&nbsp;
across all four original movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.680
is a young man with a massive weight on&nbsp;
his shoulders: His family is crumbling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.280
and he might be the only person who can save it.&nbsp;
Accomplishing this gets even more difficult when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:34.320
he's sent to mentor District 12's female tribute&nbsp;
to the 10th annual Hunger Games: Lucy Gray Baird,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.760
a gutsy musician. She wants to win, and her&nbsp;
charisma might just help her achieve this.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.120
But the Capitol is as thorny as ever, and&nbsp;
plenty of people would like to see Snow and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:50.520
Lucy burn. New characters like Casca Highbottom,&nbsp;
architect of the Games, and Dr. Volumnia Gaul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.720
head gamemaker, cast long shadows, while ancestors&nbsp;
of figures we're already familiar with, like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:01.280
Lucky Flickerman, reveal just how deeply rooted&nbsp;
Panem's dysfunction truly is. Things get even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:06.600
more complex when Snow's feelings for Lucy become&nbsp;
deeper and more urgent than simple mentorship.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.000
Despite the appearance of some familiar names,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:15.000
producer Nina Jacobson described the movie as an&nbsp;
independent entity. She remarked at CineEurope.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.680
"It's a new story, with new ground and new&nbsp;
characters. We were able to create a completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:25.040
different visual language ... one that is still&nbsp;
recognizably Panem, but also different and fresh."

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.200
It'll also be a philosophically weighty&nbsp;
tale. Jacobson mused to Polygon:

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.080
"Are we fundamentally good if left to our own&nbsp;
devices? Are we fundamentally bad and need the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.600
state to keep us in check or we'll destroy each&nbsp;
other? These ideas about how people perceive each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:43.840
other and the government, and what they need based&nbsp;
on those perceptions, felt so incredibly timely."

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:50.480
"See how quickly we become predators?&nbsp;
See how quickly civilization disappears?"

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.880
So, who's playing these songbirds&nbsp;
and snakes? First and foremost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:58.280
Tom Blyth will star as the young Coriolanus&nbsp;
Snow. It'll doubtlessly be interesting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.520
see how he fleshes out the villain&nbsp;
after Donald Sutherland's commanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:06.040
presence in the first four "Hunger Games"&nbsp;
movies. Blyth isn't hugely well known yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.400
but he's drummed up some buzz with recent&nbsp;
projects like "Billy the Kid" and the HBO&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.840
period series "The Gilded Age." His performance as&nbsp;
Snow is poised to launch him into further heights.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.080
As for Lucy Gray Baird, she'll be played by&nbsp;
"West Side Story" and "Shazam! Fury of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:25.320
Gods" star Rachel Zegler. She's already proved&nbsp;
she can handle emotional drama, thanks to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:30.120
time working with Steven Spielberg on the former&nbsp;
musical, while the latter project showcased her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:35.840
action potential. This is a perfect mix for a&nbsp;
dauntless and warm-hearted heroine like Lucy.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:40.600
The rest of the cast is just as impressive.&nbsp;
Celebrated talent Peter Dinklage will play Casca&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:46.280
Highbottom, the complex brain behind the Hunger&nbsp;
Games concept. The legendary Viola Davis will play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:51.720
Dr. Volumnia Gaul, who gets the Hunger Games well&nbsp;
and truly rolling with her sinister machinations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:57.360
Jason Schwartzman will play Lucky Flickerman,&nbsp;
ancestor to Stanley Tucci's Caesar Flickerman.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.560
Many fans have wondered if the stars of&nbsp;
the first four "Hunger Games" movies will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.680
make an appearance, particularly Jennifer&nbsp;
Lawrence. "Watch What Happens Live" host&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.920
Andy Cohen went ahead and addressed&nbsp;
a rumor she'll be popping up in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:13.120
Panem of the past as Katniss' grandma.&nbsp;
Lawrence made it clear that she will not.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.040
"No."
"That's not happening."

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.320
"That's not true."

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.320
Tough luck, Katniss fans.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:22.720
When fans settle in to watch "The Hunger Games:&nbsp;
The Ballad of Songbirds &amp; Snakes," they won't just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.200
be returning to a familiar fictional landscape&nbsp;
— they'll be returning to the work of a beloved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:32.040
director. Francis Lawrence, who directed every&nbsp;
"Hunger Games" movie except the very first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:37.080
will helm the Snow-centric prequel. Fans know&nbsp;
he's an expert when it comes to this franchise:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:40.760
His skillful, inventive, and steady&nbsp;
direction is a huge part of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:45.440
makes the original quartet work. Now,&nbsp;
he's poised to take it back in time.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:49.520
Lawrence's filmography isn't confined&nbsp;
to Panem, however. Moviegoers first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:55.640
encountered him through 2005's "Constantine,"&nbsp;
his first feature. More met him through 2007's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.640 --> 00:05:00.560
"I Am Legend." Since he guided Katniss through&nbsp;
the revolution, he's directed two more movies:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:06.040
the 2018 spy thriller "Red Sparrow" and&nbsp;
the 2022 family fantasy "Slumberland."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:10.720
He's also set to helm an adaptation of the&nbsp;
acclaimed "BioShock "video game series.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:14.720
Francis Lawrence isn't the only familiar&nbsp;
creative returning for the prequel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:18.720
Producer Nina Jacobson of the production&nbsp;
company Color Force has been producing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.480
the "Hunger Games" film series since the&nbsp;
very beginning after reading the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:27.880
book in 2009 and personally tracking down&nbsp;
Suzanne Collins to secure the film rights.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:33.120
Joining her for "The Ballad of Songbirds &amp; Snakes"&nbsp;
is fellow Color Force producer Brad Simpson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:38.120
who has worked closely with Jacobson on projects&nbsp;
such as the "Diary of a Wimpy Kid" film series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:43.080
and the "American Crime Story" anthology series.&nbsp;
Screenwriter Michael Arndt, known for films like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:48.400
"Little Miss Sunshine" and "Toy Story 3," is also&nbsp;
returning after helping pen the script for 2013's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:53.160
"The Hunger Games: Catching Fire." He and fellow&nbsp;
screenwriter Michael Lesslie are working from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:59.160
treatment by original author Suzanne Collins,&nbsp;
who is an executive producer on the project.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:05.000
"The Hunger Games: The Ballad of Songbirds &amp;&nbsp;
Snakes" has been given an MPA rating of PG-13,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:09.200
which comes as no surprise given that every&nbsp;
previous "Hunger Games" movie has earned this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:14.880
rating. However, as fans know well, things get&nbsp;
plenty dark in Panem. Characters are viciously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:19.280
murdered, and even our noblest heroes&nbsp;
are forced to commit haunting crimes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:24.080
Katniss herself ends the series by putting a&nbsp;
fatal arrow through President Coin's sternum.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.080
This new outing might take place in the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:30.400
but it's not any rosier. The trailer&nbsp;
contains glimpses of all sorts of darkness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:35.680
from a wrathful Snow repeatedly firing a rifle&nbsp;
to tributes attacking each other in the arena.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:38.960
"I want my enemies to see&nbsp;
a rainbow of destruction."

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.600
It appears as though this one is&nbsp;
going to be the darkest entry in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:47.000
the franchise yet — it's been rated PG-13&nbsp;
for "strong violent content and disturbing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:51.320
material." This phrasing is stronger than&nbsp;
that used for previous entries, which only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:55.880
warned of things like "frightening&nbsp;
images" and "thematic material."

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:59.480
To capture the unique setting of post-war&nbsp;
Panem in "The Hunger Games: The Ballad of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:03.960
Songbirds &amp; Snakes," the production went&nbsp;
abroad. Filming took place in Poland and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:09.240
Germany across several locations. Unlike the&nbsp;
Hunger Games arenas in the first three films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.600
which were newly designed and built yearly, the&nbsp;
10th Hunger Games took place in the ruins of an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:19.160
amphitheater. These bare-bones arena scenes&nbsp;
were filmed at Centennial Hall in Wrocław,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.280
a historic building made to&nbsp;
host events and concerts.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:27.480
Additional filming locations include Berlin's&nbsp;
Olympiastadion, a sports stadium constructed for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:33.800
the 1936 Summer Olympics, and the Krematorium&nbsp;
Baumschulenweg, also located in Berlin. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.640
production also made use of the Monument to&nbsp;
the Battle of the Nations in the German city&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:42.400
of Leipzig. Elsewhere in Germany, a public park&nbsp;
built on the site of an abandoned coal and steel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:49.000
production plant is doubling for District 12, as&nbsp;
unofficial photos from the set appear to confirm.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:53.880
Suzanne Collins' "The Ballad of Songbirds&nbsp;
and Snakes" comes in at 517 pages when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:58.240
you include the epilogue, making it the&nbsp;
longest book in the series. The story of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:02.440
young Coriolanus Snow's formative&nbsp;
years is divided into four parts:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:07.360
His time as a student at the Capitol's Academy,&nbsp;
being a mentor for the 10th Hunger Games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:12.440
becoming a peacekeeper, and then his reckoning.&nbsp;
The book's four-part structure lends itself well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:16.120
to a two-part movie adaptation — the&nbsp;
first part covering the events of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:20.280
Hunger Games and the second covering the&nbsp;
aftermath — but that won't be the case.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:24.560
Instead of splitting the movie into two parts like&nbsp;
they did with "Mockingjay," "The Hunger Games:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:28.200
The Ballad of Songbirds &amp; Snakes" will take&nbsp;
on the challenge of telling its story in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:35.160
single sitting, albeit a rather long one — the&nbsp;
runtime is 165 minutes in the United States,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.840
while a slightly shorter version will be&nbsp;
shown in other territories. This will make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:43.160
"The Hunger Games: The Ballad of Songbirds&nbsp;
&amp; Snakes" the longest movie in the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:46.360
taking the crown from "The&nbsp;
Hunger Games: Catching Fire."

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:49.920
"The Hunger Games: The Ballad of&nbsp;
Songbirds &amp; Snakes" takes place 64&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:54.120
years before Katniss Everdeen volunteers&nbsp;
as tribute. Although audiences are well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:58.200
aware of the origins of the Hunger&nbsp;
Games and Coriolanus Snow's future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:03.000
the upcoming prequel will offer deeper&nbsp;
insight into the already established timeline.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:06.480
For instance, the 10th Hunger Games is&nbsp;
the first to implement mentors for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:11.280
district's tributes, chosen from the&nbsp;
Academy's top students. Additionally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:15.080
the audience incentives of gambling and&nbsp;
purchasing gifts for tributes that become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:19.920
mainstays in future games are implemented&nbsp;
for the first time at the suggestion of Snow.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:24.280
"Everything is about winning. If&nbsp;
not the games now, then the crowd."

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:28.280
The film will also show glimpses into the&nbsp;
devastating war of the first rebellion and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:33.240
its immediate aftermath, taking viewers&nbsp;
even further back in the timeline.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:38.440
Music plays a crucial role in "The Ballad of&nbsp;
Songbirds and Snakes," hence the title. Lucy Gray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:42.960
Baird uses her musical talent to her advantage&nbsp;
as a way of surviving both the Hunger Games&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:48.560
and day-to-day life in District 12. As Suzanne&nbsp;
Collins explained in an interview with Scholastic:

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:52.280
"Lucy Gray's legacy is that she introduced&nbsp;
entertainment to the Hunger Games."

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:56.240
She has several original songs which&nbsp;
later become a part of Panem history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:00.840
like "The Hanging Tree," which was sung by Katniss&nbsp;
in "The Hunger Games: Mockingjay – Part 1."

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:06.680
In a Variety interview, Francis Lawrence describes&nbsp;
Suzanne Collins as a country music aficionado,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:10.920
which made finding Lucy's sound less of a&nbsp;
daunting task. The film's music producer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:15.480
Dave Cobb drew from Appalachian music,&nbsp;
and the creative team were also influenced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:20.640
by early Dolly Parton and Sissy Spacek's&nbsp;
portrayal of Loretta Lynn when shaping Lucy.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:24.240
Her version of "The Hanging Tree" can&nbsp;
be heard in the second official trailer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:28.600
According to Nina Jacobson, this song and&nbsp;
others are performed by Rachel Zegler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:31.640
who opted to sing them live&nbsp;
without playback during filming.

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:38.920
"We also knew that once we had her on set, Rachel&nbsp;
really could do it. It's just so easy for her."

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:42.320
Nine-time Oscar nominee James Newton&nbsp;
Howard is returning to compose the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:46.360
score as he did for the previous&nbsp;
films in the "Hunger Games" series.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:50.680
Coming back to a franchise eight years after&nbsp;
its last installment with an entirely new set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:54.680
of characters can be intimidating, but&nbsp;
the creatives behind "The Hunger Games:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:59.400
The Ballad of Songbirds &amp; Snakes" were up for&nbsp;
the challenge. Francis Lawrence told Collider:

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.800
"It very much feels like a Hunger Games movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:06.360
but at the same time feels really fresh&nbsp;
and unique, and thematically unique."

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:10.120
As for the approach to the new characters,&nbsp;
Lawrence and Nina Jacobson believe they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:15.880
captivating in their own right. When describing&nbsp;
Lucy Gray Baird to Variety, Jacobson explained,

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:19.880
"She's such a different character from&nbsp;
Katniss. She's such a performer. Katniss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:23.520
is the opposite. This is a woman&nbsp;
who loves and lives to perform."

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:27.160
"What is that dress? Is she some sort of clown?"

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.280
Snow, on the other hand, posed some challenges for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:33.080
Lawrence. He explained his thought&nbsp;
process to Empire, questioning,

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.920
"How do we make this person that's&nbsp;
going to be the antagonist of our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:40.600
story the protagonist of our story? How can&nbsp;
we get audiences behind him in his struggle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:44.640
and see him change and be groomed and&nbsp;
turned into the Snow of the later series?"

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:48.800
Lawrence also revealed to Entertainment&nbsp;
Weekly that Tom Blyth was advised to refrain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:54.360
from watching early Donald Sutherland movies and&nbsp;
embrace his own interpretation of the character.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:59.640
In the literary world, readers regard Suzanne&nbsp;
Collins as a highly private person who rarely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:03.880
participates in interviews and lacks&nbsp;
a social media presence. It's unknown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:07.920
whether she will expand on the world of Panem&nbsp;
with another "Hunger Games" book, but she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:13.040
yet to dismiss the idea altogether. It's just&nbsp;
a matter of finding the right topic and angle.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.920
Speaking to Polygon, Nina Jacobson said that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:19.280
doesn't think Collins is done&nbsp;
with Panem just yet, saying:

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:22.080
"Do I think she will write&nbsp;
more books in the world? I do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:26.040
and I hope she will. Do I have any&nbsp;
idea what they'll be? Not really!"

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:30.920
"It's a mystery, and mysteries&nbsp;
have a way of driving people mad."

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:34.800
One thing's for sure — Collins won't write&nbsp;
another Panem-set book just because there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:38.800
money to be made. Francis Lawrence told&nbsp;
Entertainment Weekly the main reason why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:43.560
he and Jacobson stand behind her if she&nbsp;
chooses to revisit the series, saying:

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:49.440
"Suzanne always writes from a thematic foundation.&nbsp;
If she has something to say, I want to hear it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:53.701
I'm fascinated by her perspective. I&nbsp;
will always want to follow her lead."

